    "result_text": "All 52 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `Cp38Tests`.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe change rejects a `POST /api/owners` request with **400 Bad Request** when the owner's email domain is on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (not Spring MVC), I added:\n\n1. **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** (function step) \u2014 reads the published `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, extracts the domain after the last `@`, and throws when it's blocklisted. Email is optional, so absent/domain-less values pass through untouched. The domain match is case-insensitive (and `ValidateOwnerFields` already lower-cases the email).\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** \u2014 a checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause and routes to escalation handling).\n\n3. **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the existing handler style (`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`, etc.).\n\n4. **Wired the new step into `owners.POST.yml`** right after `validate` (so the email is already normalized) and before the other business-rule rejections, keeping `govern: [ transaction ]` consistent with the surrounding steps.\n\nThe test `Cp38Tests` (posting `x@mailinator.com` and expecting 400) passes, and the full suite remains green \u2014 no regressions.",
